 protocols="# Step16 protocol\n\nNo training. Original artifacts are read only. Every new file uses exclusive creation; completed phases skip only after all recorded output hashes verify. All registered prediction-source hashes are checked again at completion. Inputs with altered hashes stop resume.\n\nPrimary O neural DW uses B5FIX seed42 plus B5 other seeds. Archived neural seed42 appears only in original-submission reference artifacts. Available O neural Daily/Weekly-only archive cells are reference-only because no B5FIX replacements exist; never merge them into the primary B multiplicity family. Deterministic predictors have n=1. Available primary single-resolution controls have n=1; SD(ddof1) is undefined. The optional scope questions were unanswered when defaults were fixed; their recommended choices are recorded in scope_decisions.json.\n\nLoss=first−second, negative favors first. IC=first−second. Paired seeds use sorted order 0,1,21,42,3407. Each joint replicate draws5 paired seeds with replacement then common overlapping noncircular date blocks L=h, B=20000. Date-only results condition on the observed seeds. Missing IC dates retain391-calendar positions and average paired-valid dates within seed, using the imported Step15 branch. Seed-by-date matrices use the same contiguous layout as Step9/15; this matters only for floating-point ties at bootstrap-p thresholds. RNG entropy and actual common draws are in RNG_MANIFEST.json and rng/.\n\nSquared-loss/IC comparisons use two-sided centered bootstrap p with +1 correction and percentile95% CI, imported from Step5. CW uses Step5 f, one-sided centered MBB and normal Newey–West p, with lag h−1 unchanged. IC uses Newey–West lag h, two-sided centered MBB p. Four R2 values are descriptive; associated flag p is CW vs Global Train-Mean only and does not test R2 relative to Zero/ticker/expanding references. Expanding mean is the existing pooled predictor using only labels with target_date<=anchor_date. Holm covers3 horizons within contrast×metric×input family (also window/backbone/method/seed where applicable). B primary adjustments cover all708 primary cells separately for CW-NW, CW-MBB, IC-MBB; no post-selection family. Reference raw diagnostics are separate.\n\nBenchmark DataLoaders use original global RNG (generator=None); PathFormer mechanisms use generator42. H is sequential CPU intra12/inter12, OMP_NUM_THREADS unset, OMP_DYNAMIC=FALSE, MKL_DYNAMIC=FALSE before torch. Full-checkpoint TEST I0 and Step15-cache I0 must both be EXACT(<1e-7) before I1–I6. C uses the Step13/Stage3a core.load_causal binding. The original Step9 intervention functions and original model/aggregation/head are reused. Existing O four seeds are replayed as well to recover date-level series for the five-seed joint analysis. No model is fit or changed.\n\nAll other statistics use deterministic stored predictions, imported Step5/7/7B functions, and source-adapted original inline bootstrap blocks. Source excerpts are saved, rather than reimplementing formulas. Step8 allocation/simulation/cost functions and its strategy loop are reused; top3, long/short tests, alpha tests and extra contrasts are disabled. GRS uses existing gamma5/cost10 all-seed and ensemble groups per input/h; C includes Ridge. Top5 and gamma1/2/5/10/20, cap25%, costs0/5/10/20bp, 252-session Ledoit–Wolf, t+1 close and nonoverlap are unchanged. No covariance regularizer is added to GRS.\n\nC rolling subgroups are descriptive only. Each stock's trailing60-session simple-return volatility uses ddof1; tercile cutpoints use that window TRAIN anchor observations only. Ties: low<=q33, mid<=q67, high otherwise. Test halves have195/196 dates. Cross-sectional IC for a single-stock/date group is undefined, retained as N/A; no temporal Spearman is substituted. Group means/SD average seed-level metrics, never predictions, except explicitly named ensembles. B3 versus formal combines coverage and unfinished-week exclusion and for C the changed reference price. Step15 secondary head-retrained results are excluded.\n\nTest accounting counts reported inferential rows and requested IC-NW t-only rows. Holm adjustments are not additional tests; confidence intervals without a null test are not additional tests. Superseded numerical/review attempts do not introduce new hypotheses; retained intermediate tables are not primary. Duplicated table views are labelled separately in TEST_LEDGER. Historical frozen/financial/portfolio test statistics shown for reference are counted separately from newly calculated tests. Bootstrap replay and thread-sensitivity checks verify existing statistics rather than adding hypotheses.\n"
